[about]
Title=03 - Key Patterns
Intro=The rules every EdSharp key follows, so a key can be guessed before it is learned: the word gives the letter, Control does, Alt says, Shift widens, Alt Shift is a command with no control, the function keys follow Windows -- and the keys that explain the keys.
Setup=EdSharp is open on an empty document.
Homework=Guess the key for Replace, Save As and Thesaurus before you look them up, then check with Control plus F1.

[step]

Say=Every key in EdSharp is named for a word in its command: Control plus O is Open, Control plus S is Save, Control plus F is Find, Control plus K is bookmark, F7 is spell check as in Word. A key never comes from the middle of a word.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus a letter does something. Alt plus a letter says something and changes nothing: Alt plus A the address, Alt plus Z the status, Alt plus P the path, Alt plus Y the yield -- the count of characters, words and lines.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Adding Shift widens or reverses a key. Control plus O opens a file; Control plus Shift plus O opens one in another format, converting it to text. Control plus F finds forward; Control plus Shift plus F finds backward. F3 finds the next; Shift plus F3 the previous.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus a letter is a command with no control of its own: Alt plus Shift plus E exports the document as another format, Alt plus Shift plus H shows the hotkey summary.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The function keys follow Windows and Office: F1 help, F3 find again, F4 the open documents, F5 run, F7 spelling, F11 the newer version, F12 the AI. Control plus F5 compiles; Control plus Shift plus F5 chooses the compiler.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The keys that explain the keys. Control plus F1 is the Key Describer: on, every key says what it does instead of doing it, the safe way to explore the keyboard. Alt plus F10 is the Alternate Menu: every command in one list you type into, and the list tells you the key.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Hear=Command, list box, 1 of 222

[step]

Say=Type the word convert.
Key=convert
Hear=Convert File Format, Control plus Shift plus V, 1 of 9
Say=Nine commands with convert in the name, and the first one gives you its key. That is how a key is learned here.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the menu without running anything. Hotkeys, in the Help menu, lists every key three ways; and your reader's own Insert plus Tab says where you are.
Key=Escape
Hear=Untitled, edit, multiline, blank

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus F10.
Key=
Hear=Alternate Menu

[step]

Say=Control plus F1.
Key=
Hear=Key Describer
